#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:305
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:307
msgid ""
"When using GitHub, Read the Docs uses a GitHub App to interact with your "
"repositories. This has the following benefits over using an OAuth "
"application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:310
msgid ""
"More control over which repositories Read the Docs can access. You don't "
"need to grant access to all your repositories in order to create an "
"account or connect a project to a single repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:312
msgid ""
"No need to create webhooks on your repositories. The GitHub App "
"subscribes to all required events when you install it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:314
msgid ""
"No need to create a deploy key on your repository (|com_brand| only). The"
" GitHub App can clone your private repositories using a temporary token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:316
msgid ""
"If the original user who connected the repository to Read the Docs loses "
"access to the project or repository, the GitHub App will still have "
"access to the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:318
msgid ""
"You can revoke access to the GitHub App at any time from your GitHub "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:319
msgid ""
"Never out of sync with changes on your repository. The GitHub App "
"subscribes to all required events and will always keep your project up to"
" date with your repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:322
msgid ""
"The following features are only available for projects connected through "
"the GitHub App:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:324
msgid ""
":ref:`Build overview comment on pull requests <visual-diff:Show build "
"overview in pull requests>`, with a link to the preview and the list of "
"files changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:326
msgid ""
":ref:`Webhook filters <automation-rules:Webhook filters>` in automation "
"rules, for example to :doc:`skip builds </guides/build/skip-or-cancel-"
"builds>` when no documentation files changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:330
msgid "Adding a project from a repository"
msgstr ""

