" want to connect from the :guilabel:`Connected repository` dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:359
msgid "Manually migrating a project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:361
msgid ""
"We recommend using the migration page to migrate your projects from the "
"old OAuth application to the new GitHub App."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:363
msgid ""
"`Read the Docs Community <https://app.readthedocs.org/accounts/migrate-"
"to-github-app/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:364
msgid ""
"`Read the Docs Business <https://app.readthedocs.com/accounts/migrate-to-"
"github-app/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:366
msgid ""
"But in case you need to manually migrate a project, you can follow these "
"steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:369
msgid ""
"Go to your Read the Docs project's :menuselection:`Settings --> "
"Integrations`, and delete all the integrations that are listed there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:371
msgid ""
"Go to the settings page of your GitHub repository, click on the GitHub "
":guilabel:`Webhooks` tab, and delete all the webhooks with URLs that "
"start with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:374
msgid ""
"``https://readthedocs.org/api/v2/webhook/<your-project-slug>`` or "
"``https://app.readthedocs.org/api/v2/webhook/<your-project-slug>`` for "
"Read the Docs Community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:375
msgid ""
"``https://readthedocs.com/api/v2/webhook/<your-project-slug>`` or "
"``https://app.readthedocs.com/api/v2/webhook/<your-project-slug>`` for "
"Read the Docs Business."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:377
msgid ""
"For projects using Read the Docs Business, go to the settings page of "
"your GitHub repository, click on the GitHub :guilabel:`Deploy keys` tab, "
"and delete the deploy key with a title matching the format "
"``support@readthedocs.com (<your-project-slug>)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:380
msgid ""
":ref:`Connect the project to the repository <reference/git-"
"integration:Connect a repository to an existing project>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:383
msgid "Revoking access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:387
msgid ""
"If you revoke access to the GitHub App with any of the methods below, all"
" projects linked to that repository will stop working, but the projects "
"and their documentation will still be available. If you grant access to "
"the repository again, you will need to :ref:`manually connect your "
"project to the repository <reference/git-integration:Connect a repository"
" to an existing project>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:393
msgid ""
"You can revoke access to the Read the Docs GitHub App at any time from "
"your GitHub settings. All revocation options happen from your **account "
"or organization settings**; no action is required inside Read the Docs "
"until you decide to reconnect a project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:399
msgid "There are three ways to revoke access to the Read the Docs GitHub App:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:401
msgid "Revoke access to one or more repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:402
msgid ""
"Remove the repositories from the list of repositories that the GitHub App"
" has access to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:403
msgid "Suspend the GitHub App:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:404
msgid ""
"This will suspend the GitHub App and revoke access to all repositories. "
"The installation and configuration will still be available, and you can "
"re-enable the GitHub App at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:407
msgid "Uninstall the GitHub App:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:408
msgid ""
"This will uninstall the GitHub App and revoke access to all repositories."
" The installation and configuration will be removed, and you will need to"
" re-install the GitHub App and reconfigure it to use it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:413
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:415
msgid ""
"When cloning private repositories (|com_brand| only) Read the Docs "
"creates an `installation access token "
"<https://docs.github.com/en/rest/apps/apps?apiVersion=2022-11-28#create-"
"an-installation-access-token-for-an-app>`__, which has read access to the"
" `contents permission <https://docs.github.com/en/rest/authentication"
"/permissions-required-for-github-apps?apiVersion=2022-11-28#repository-"
"permissions-for-contents>`__, and it's scoped to the repository to be "
"cloned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:420
msgid ""
"This token is valid for one hour and GitHub automatically grants read "
"access to the `metadata permission "
"<https://docs.github.com/en/rest/authentication/permissions-required-for-"
"github-apps?apiVersion=2022-11-28#repository-permissions-for-"
"metadata>`__, which allows querying the repository collaborators, events,"
" and other metadata. By default, Read the Docs doesn't show this token "
"during the build, but the token is available during the whole build "
"process. Make sure to not print it in your build logs, and that only "
"trusted users are able to trigger builds on your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:429
msgid ""
"If your repository is public, Read the Docs will not create an "
"installation access token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:433
msgid ""
"The build log page is publicly accessible only if your project and "
"version to build are marked as public. See more in :doc:`/commercial"
"/privacy-level`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:437
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:439
msgid "Repository not found in the repository list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:440
msgid ""
"Make sure you have installed the corresponding GitHub App in your GitHub "
"account or organization, and have granted access to the repository your "
"project will be connected to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:446
msgid ""
"If you still can't see the repository in the list, you may need to wait a"
" couple of minutes and refresh the page, or click on the \"Refresh your "
"repositories\" button on the project creation page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:450
msgid "Installation on an organization is pending"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:451
msgid ""
"If you aren't an owner of the GitHub organization, GitHub sends an "
"installation request to the organization owners instead of installing the"
" app. Read the Docs can't access the organization's repositories until an"
" owner approves the request. See GitHub's docs on `requesting a GitHub "
"App for your organization <https://docs.github.com/en/apps/using-github-"
"apps/requesting-a-github-app-from-your-organization-owner>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:456
msgid "Repository is in the list, but isn't usable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:457
msgid ""
"Make sure you have admin access to the repository you are trying to use "
"for your project. If you are using |org_brand|, make sure your project is"
" public, or use |com_brand| to create projects from private repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/git-integration.rst:461
msgid ""
"If you still can't use the repository for your project, you may need to "
"wait a couple of minutes and refresh the page, or click on the \"Refresh "
"your repositories\" button on the project creation page."
msgstr ""

